Third-Party Standards, Specifications, and Data Notices
================================================================================

This software includes, references, or derives data contracts from the following
third-party specifications and international financial messaging standards:

1. ISO 20022 Universal Financial Industry Message Scheme
   - Organization: International Organization for Standardization (ISO) / ISO 20022 Registration Authority
   - Message Definition: pacs.008.001.10 (Financial Institutional Customer Credit Transfer)
   - Source: https://www.iso20022.org
   - Intellectual Property Policy: The ISO 20022 message definitions and XML schemas are free of intellectual
     property rights and open for use by any interested party in the financial services industry.
   - Files: schemas/finance/pacs_008_core.xsd, data/pacs_008_customer_credit_transfer.xml

2. ISO 4217 Currency and Funds Code List
   - Published by the International Organization for Standardization (ISO).
   - Usage: Currency code enumeration identifiers (USD, EUR, GBP, etc.).

3. FedNow Instant Payment Telemetry Formats
   - Format: Synthetic $250,000 USD B2B supplier payment payload modeled after modern instant payment
     settlement mechanisms and Stripe PaymentIntent structures.
   - Purpose: Provided solely for compatibility, testing, and interoperability demonstration.
   - Files: data/payment_intent_fednow.json, schemas/payments/payment-service.proto

